💰 Expense Tracker for Kids

A simple and interactive Expense Tracker Web Application designed to help children learn the basics of personal finance and money management. The application allows users to record their income and expenses, monitor their current balance, and review their transaction history in real time.

The project focuses on providing a clear and beginner-friendly interface so that young users can easily understand how money flows in and out. By using this tool, children can begin developing healthy financial habits such as tracking spending, saving money, and understanding how expenses affect their balance.

This project also serves as a learning exercise for beginner developers, demonstrating how to build a dynamic web application using fundamental web technologies.

---

🎯 Project Objective

Financial literacy is an essential life skill, yet many young people are not introduced to money management concepts early enough. This Expense Tracker is designed to simplify these concepts through an interactive and easy-to-use interface.

The main goals of the project are:

* Introduce children to basic financial concepts such as income, expenses, and balance.
* Help users visualize how spending affects savings.
* Encourage responsible money habits through simple tracking.
* Provide a hands-on example of a real-world web application for beginners learning programming.

By interacting with the application, children can better understand how managing money works in everyday life.

---

🖥️ Application Overview

The Expense Tracker interface is divided into three main sections that help users monitor and manage their finances effectively.

-- 1. Balance Overview Dashboard

At the top of the application, users can see a financial summary dashboard displaying their overall financial status.

The dashboard contains three important elements:

--- Current Balance

The balance shows the total amount of money remaining after calculating all recorded income and expenses.

Balance is calculated using the formula:

```
Balance = Total Income − Total Expenses
```

This helps users understand how their spending affects their remaining money.

--- Total Income

The income section displays the total amount of money received.

Examples of income may include:

* Pocket money
* Allowance
* Gift money
* Rewards or small earnings

Income values are displayed separately so users can clearly see how much money they have earned.

--- Total Expenses

The expenses section shows the total amount of money spent.

Common examples include:

* Buying toys
* Snacks or food
* School supplies
* Entertainment purchases

Tracking expenses helps children understand where their money is going.

---

-- 2. Transaction History

The transaction history section lists all financial activities recorded by the user.

Each transaction entry includes:

* Description – A short explanation of the transaction
* Amount – The value of money involved in the transaction

Examples of transactions may include:

| Description        | Amount |
| ------------------ | ------ |
| Salary / Allowance | +500   |
| Toy Purchase       | -200   |
| Snacks             | -50    |
| Gift Money         | +300   |

Positive amounts represent income, while negative amounts represent expenses.

The transaction list helps users:

* Review previous financial activities
* Identify spending habits
* Understand how different transactions impact their balance

---

-- 3. Add Transaction Section

The application includes a simple form that allows users to add new financial transactions.

The form contains two fields:

--- Description Field

Users enter a short description explaining the purpose of the transaction.

Examples:

```
Buy Toy
Pocket Money
Ice Cream
School Supplies
```

--- Amount Field

The amount determines whether the transaction is income or expense.

Rules:

```
Positive number  → Income
Negative number → Expense
```

Examples:

```
500   → Income
-200  → Expense
```

After filling in the details, the user clicks the Add Transaction button.

When a transaction is added:

1. The transaction appears in the transaction history.
2. The income or expense totals are updated automatically.
3. The overall balance recalculates in real time.

---

⚙️ Core Features

--- Real-Time Balance Updates

The system automatically recalculates the balance, income, and expenses whenever a new transaction is added.

---Transaction Tracking

Users can maintain a complete record of all financial activities.

---Simple and Child-Friendly Interface

The application design is intentionally minimal and easy to understand so that children can use it without confusion.

---Financial Awareness

The project encourages users to:

* Monitor spending
* Develop saving habits
* Understand budgeting basics

---

🧮 Example Use Case

Suppose a child receives $500 as pocket money.

They spend:

* $200 on toys
* $100 on snacks

The tracker will display:

```
Income: $500
Expenses: $300
Balance: $200
```

This helps the child understand that spending reduces the available balance, encouraging better financial decisions.

